HyPhy reads a FASTA alignment of sequences of different lengths without a
word. This entry point, appended to HyPhy's main file, refuses it, seeds
HyPhy's random numbers with --bc-seed and, natively, finds HyPhy's batch
files next to the executable.

HyPhy seeded its random numbers with the time and its process ID, so its
optimizers started from other points in every run and found other fits.
The seed is now --bc-seed's, 1 by default.

